#
# ONE CONCEPT: a factory parameter is by-name, `_x: => T`, and the FACTORY BODY IS ITS PRELUDE. A
# bodiless factory already binds each parameter once as the instance's `override lazy val x = _x`;
# a bodied one reads `_x` inside the lazy members it authors. So an argument is evaluated on first
# read and never if unused — `Present(sys.error(…))` constructs, and reading `value` twice evaluates
# the argument once (PresenceTest, 623 tests). `now par` keeps `_x: T`; the corpus needs it nowhere:
# no factory apply meets a host signature or is passed as a function value (grepped `.apply` bare,
# `map(X)`, `forProduct`: none; every decoder CALLS apply in its yield).
#
